    <GaugingStation location="Brydekirk" name="Annan" number="78003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station. Natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Gauged up to 3.7m (453cumecs, about 1.5 QMED); good performance at high flows. Ratings derived from current meter gaugings. Simple extrapolation of the rating curve.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station with cableway (span 190 feet) located on straight section below bend and with slightly curving channel below.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural flow regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Silurain shales in the north; Carboniferous series in the south. Centre of catchment is dominated by Triassic sandstone aquifer of the Lochmaben basin, with a smaller ribbon aquifer extending up the valley to Moffat. Rural catchment, some arable land use, mostly pasture and forestry. Motorway built during station record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged well above QMED, good performance at high flows." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
